WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.302
[music playing]

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.903
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
After a rough voyage,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.473
we've arrived at the end
of the Tracy Arm Fjord

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.909
to search for glacial ice.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:10.844
Oh my god.
It's so--

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.878
GORDON RAMSAY: What a journey.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:12.712
--gorgeous.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.114
GORDON RAMSAY: It's beautiful.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.749
So we're looking for what size?

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.551
So what we want to look for is
something that's very rounded.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.986
GORDON RAMSAY: Right.
What about that one?

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.287
That's a--
- No, Gordon.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.589
I don't think that
one's going to work.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.790
That's like your
own private island.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:24.591
Wow.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.625
Look at that thing.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.694
Let's try this one
here to the left--

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:31.564
the white one at 11:00.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.733
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
10,000 years in the making,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.537
these glaciers produce
the purest ice imaginable.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.938
I like that one.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:42.041
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Perfect for cocktails.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.878
GORDON RAMSAY: So the
secret behind this is--

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.413
Screwing.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.614
[laughs]

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.382
GORDON RAMSAY: Screwing
these into the big block.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.550
Yes.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.452
And then after that we're
going to hook it up,

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.953
and we're going to
hoist it on board.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.422
Got you.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.524
This is the most work I've
ever done [bleep] an ice cube

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.858
in my entire life.
- [laughs]

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.593
I hope this is going to
make the best cocktail.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.528
It's going to be fabulous.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.862
Just trust me.
GORDON RAMSAY: Right.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.063
You ready?
- Yes.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.500
OK, start screwing.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.469
We're going to hook
it up to a D-ring.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:12.572
And if it's not all the way in,
it's going to crack the ice.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.407
You have to kind of be,
like, over the water,

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.075
you know, so you're
on top of it.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.444
[bleep]

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.446
Let's just make sure
they're really down deep.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.480
Are you kidding me, Michelle?

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.714
They can't get any
further in there.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.582
OK, let's just test.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.416
Holy [bleep].

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.484
Fingers are [bleep] freezing.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:25.285
See, look.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.119
Yours is coming out.

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:26.920
Mine's coming out?

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:27.854
Yeah.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.022
You've got to get
that in deeper.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.056
Deeper?

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.391
Yeah, you're not
all the way in.

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:33.927
When we pull that up on the
winch, it's going to crack.

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.096
[bleep]

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.064
Perfect.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:43.369
[winch sounds]

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.271
[laughs]

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:47.607
GORDON RAMSAY: Stop.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.242
Stop, stop.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.143
Good job.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.512
[laughter]

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.413
That was fun.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.881
GORDON RAMSAY: Amazing.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.282
So you take that
outer layer off.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:59.152
And then you get to some
of those ice diamonds.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.453
GORDON RAMSAY: Look at this.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.421
Oh, that's gorgeous.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.121
GORDON RAMSAY: That
is so beautiful.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:02.922
Right?

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.090
Look at that formation.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.358
Should we put that in a glass?

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.159
Shall we?

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.327
You got it in there?

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.127
Wow.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.295
Ooh, I like how that--

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.230
And what do you think--

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.198
throw a little Scotch?

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:12.999
That's a good one.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.170
And now we need a
little vermouth.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:26.913
I feel like one
of the luckiest

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:28.681
mixologists anywhere
on the planet.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.383
[laughter]

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.217
Oh my lord.

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.018
Look at that.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.686
Look at the colors.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.888
I think we've earned it.
GORDON RAMSAY: Cheers.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.155
Good health.
- Cheers.

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.557
GORDON RAMSAY: Look at that.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:38.458
What an ice cube.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.225
Oh my lord.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.132
[coughs]

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:46.933
[laughs]

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.102
[bleep] That's strong.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.203
I think it's 110 proof.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.571
- [coughs]
- Cheers.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:52.539
Amazing.

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.040
Well done.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.875
I have bars, but I've
never, ever touched an ice

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.177
cube that's that perfect.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.114
And it just tasted so clean
and fresh, and slightly

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.884
effervescent in a way
that it was almost

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:10.723
lightly sort of carbonated.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.894
And a great way, I think,
to toast the beginning

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:17.964
of this incredible cook,
with an amazing cocktail

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.500
laced with glacier ice cubes.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.836
[music playing]

